("1","1","Faculty","Dear Faculty members It was already informed that our school will open on 11th and will run only morning session on the first day.From 12th onwards two sessions.Every member should attend the school on 11th.","09-06-2025","0"),
("2","2","All","Dear students  It was already informed that our school will open on 11th and will run only morning session on the first day.From 12th onwards two sessions.Every body should attend the school on 11th.","09-06-2025","0"),
("3","3","Faculty","Dear faculty members ,most of the teachers are not entering the attendance in the App both teachers attendance and emplee attendance also.It is mandatory to enter in both register and app so that we can communicate to parents in time","16-06-2025","0"),
("4","4","Student","Dear victory students ,Complete the home works given to you for these two days holidays and punishments given by the teachers.It is your responsibility ","29-06-2025","0"),
("5","5","Student","Dear students update our school app once again as there are some important updates available in the new version .You can use multiple accounts wth the same phone","07-07-2025","0"),
("6","6","10_CLASS_A","Dear 10th students Several of 10th students   are not watching and following the home works .Dont know if there are any issues in app .","09-07-2025","0");
INSERT INTO posts VALUES
("1","Building Morning Habits for a Fresh Start","Mornings set the tone for the whole day. A small positive routine can boost focus, confidence, and happiness in students.","A good morning routine is the foundation for success in school and life. Parents can play a vital role by helping their children wake up 15 minutes earlier, do light stretching or breathing exercises, and have a healthy breakfast. This calm start reduces stress, builds discipline, and improves concentration in class. Even reading a short story or practicing gratitude in the morning creates positive energy for the entire day.","cover_1.jpg","[]","","School","Admin","2025-09-02 19:26:00",""),
("2","Reducing Exam Stress at Home","Exams can feel stressful, but the right support from home makes a world of difference.","When exam season arrives, children often feel pressure to perform. Parents can ease this by ensuring study sessions are balanced with short breaks, encouraging outdoor activity, and promoting regular sleep schedules. More importantly, instead of focusing only on marks, parents should praise effort and persistence. Avoid comparing children with others-this lowers confidence. A calm, supportive home environment allows students to approach exams with focus and positivity.","cover_2.jpg","[]","","School","Admin","2025-09-02 19:27:00",""),
("3","Digital Balance: Healthy Screen Time Rules","Screens are part of modern life, but balance is the key to healthy growth.","From online classes to entertainment, screens are everywhere. Too much screen time can affect eyesight, sleep, and social skills. Parents should establish simple rules-like finishing homework before entertainment, having device-free meals, and setting bedtime \"no gadget\" zones. Children learn more from what they see than what they hear, so parents must also follow these rules to set the right example.","cover_3.jpg","[]","","School","Admin","2025-09-02 19:28:00",""),
("26","TEACHERS DAY 2025","In India, Teacher\'s Day is celebrated on September 5th to commemorate the birth anniversary of Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan.","<p class=\"MsoNormal\">In India, Teacher\'s Day is celebrated on September 5th to commemorate the birth anniversary of Dr. Sarvepalli Radhakrishnan, a revered scholar, philosopher, and the second President of India. When his students approached him in 1962 to celebrate his birthday, he humbly requested that the day be dedicated to honoring the contributions of all teachers across the country.<o:p></o:p></p>INSERT INTO posts_03_09_2025 VALUES
("1","1","Building Morning Habits for a Fresh Start","Mornings set the tone for the whole day. A small positive routine can boost focus, confidence, and happiness in students.","A good morning routine is the foundation for success in school and life. Parents can play a vital role by helping their children wake up 15 minutes earlier, do light stretching or breathing exercises, and have a healthy breakfast. This calm start reduces stress, builds discipline, and improves concentration in class. Even reading a short story or practicing gratitude in the morning creates positive energy for the entire day.","cover_1.jpg","","","School","31-08-2025 15:33:40"),
("2","2","Reducing Exam Stress at Home","Exams can feel stressful, but the right support from home makes a world of difference.","When exam season arrives, children often feel pressure to perform. Parents can ease this by ensuring study sessions are balanced with short breaks, encouraging outdoor activity, and promoting regular sleep schedules. More importantly, instead of focusing only on marks, parents should praise effort and persistence. Avoid comparing children with others-this lowers confidence. A calm, supportive home environment allows students to approach exams with focus and positivity.","cover_2.jpg","","","School","31-08-2025 15:34:20"),
("3","3","Digital Balance: Healthy Screen Time Rules","Screens are part of modern life, but balance is the key to healthy growth.","From online classes to entertainment, screens are everywhere. Too much screen time can affect eyesight, sleep, and social skills. Parents should establish simple rules-like finishing homework before entertainment, having device-free meals, and setting bedtime \"no gadget\" zones. Children learn more from what they see than what they hear, so parents must also follow these rules to set the right example.","cover_3.jpg","","","School","31-08-2025 15:35:22");
